        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96412244?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes the sidebar group macro on the <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code> page from <code class=\"notranslate\">{{APIRef(\"DOM\")}}</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">{{APIRef(\"HTML DOM\")}}</code>, so the sidebar shows \"HTML DOM API\" instead of the misleading \"Document Object Model (DOM)\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#window\" rel=\"nofollow\">HTML Standard: the <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code> object</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-window\" rel=\"nofollow\">DOM Standard interfaces list</a> (does not include <code class=\"notranslate\">Window</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45123.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5146323062\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45123\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45123/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45123\">#45123</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45129",
            "title": "Fix incorrect sidebar group on Window pages",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-15T00:43:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T02:49:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "maitreyi03",
                "url": "https://github.com/maitreyi03"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96412244?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrects an invalid CSS media feature name in the <code class=\"notranslate\">@custom-media</code> example. The example used <code class=\"notranslate\">not (script)</code>, but <code class=\"notranslate\">script</code> is not a valid media feature, it should be <code class=\"notranslate\">not (scripting)</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@media/scripting\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">scripting</code> media feature reference</a> for the valid feature name and its accepted values.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45125.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5147382743\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45125\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45125/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45125\">#45125</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45127",
            "title": "Fix incorrect media feature name in @custom-media example",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T02:39:05.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T02:37:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "maitreyi03",
                "url": "https://github.com/maitreyi03"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43412.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4063297756\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43412/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43412\">#43412</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family</code> page listed <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> as a plain generic-family keyword, but per the CSS Fonts 4 spec the script-specific generic font families use the functional <code class=\"notranslate\">generic()</code> syntax: <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(fangsong)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(kai)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(khmer-mul)</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">generic(nastaliq)</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Syntax section: <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: fangsong;</code> → <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: generic(fangsong);</code>.</li>\n<li>Values section: replaced the bare <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> bullet with the four script-specific <code class=\"notranslate\">generic()</code> families, described per the spec, with a note that they are not yet supported by any browser.</li>\n<li>Examples: removed the fangsong live-example block, since no browser supports the value.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page previously suggested <code class=\"notranslate\">fangsong</code> was a usable keyword value, which is not the case: the bare keyword is not in the current spec grammar, and no browser supports these values.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45124",
            "title": "docs: use generic() syntax for script-specific font families",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T08:21:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-14T01:44:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "fufu1209",
                "url": "https://github.com/fufu1209"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Marionette documentation moved from <code class=\"notranslate\">firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/testing/marionette/</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">/remote/marionette/</code>, and the old URLs now return a 301 to the new location. This updates the four affected links across three Firefox release notes pages.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Two of the links carry anchors (<code class=\"notranslate\">#marionette-navigate-after-click-timeout</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">#marionette-navigate-after-click-enabled</code>); both still resolve on the new page.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The links currently redirect rather than resolving directly.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45119",
            "title": "Update Marionette documentation links to their new location",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-13T10:03:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-13T10:01:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fixes five anchor links in the DOM events table that point to sections which no longer exist.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Document</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLElement</code> used to list their events in categorized subsections, so anchors such as <code class=\"notranslate\">Document#keyboard_events</code> resolved. Both pages now use a single <code class=\"notranslate\">Events</code> section, leaving those fragments pointing at nothing. This changes them to <code class=\"notranslate\">#events</code>, which is already how the rest of this table links (<code class=\"notranslate\">AbortSignal#events</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">WebSocket#events</code>, and so on).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In each case the target section does document the events the row describes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Clipboard → <code class=\"notranslate\">Document#events</code> lists <code class=\"notranslate\">copy</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">cut</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">paste</code>.</li>\n<li>Drag → <code class=\"notranslate\">Document#events</code> lists <code class=\"notranslate\">drag</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">dragstart</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">dragend</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">drop</code>, and the rest.</li>\n<li>Inputs → <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLElement#events</code> lists <code class=\"notranslate\">input</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">change</code>.</li>\n<li>Keyboard → <code class=\"notranslate\">Document#events</code> lists <code class=\"notranslate\">keydown</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">keypress</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">keyup</code>.</li>\n<li>Network/Connection → <code class=\"notranslate\">NetworkInformation#event_handler</code> becomes <code class=\"notranslate\">#events</code>, matching the heading on that page, which documents the <code class=\"notranslate\">change</code> event.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Other broken anchors in this table are left alone: they point at event categories the target interfaces do not currently document, so repointing them would resolve the link without taking the reader anywhere useful.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These links currently drop the reader at the top of the target page rather than at the events they were sent to find.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45117",
            "title": "Fix broken anchors in the DOM events table",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-14T17:25:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-13T09:34:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62324847?u=305f6e3037692f1c5d10cb4b96403e28a427f737&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45107.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5134611355\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45107\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45107/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45107\">#45107</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">flex-flow</code> page's example was only a CSS stub. This PR turns it into a complete live example (HTML + CSS + <code class=\"notranslate\">{{EmbedLiveSample}}</code>) demonstrating <code class=\"notranslate\">flex-flow: column-reverse wrap</code>, following the structure used by the <code class=\"notranslate\">flex-direction</code> page.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45115",
            "title": "Add live example to flex-flow page",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-13T07:50:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-13T07:43:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "fufu1209",
                "url": "https://github.com/fufu1209"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109454414?u=8f40c1c1b5f0a5af5171c0cc286f21fed7097a0c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5091109058\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45048\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45048/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45048\">#45048</a>: No Browser Implements screenX, screenY according to the spec</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Changed files</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">files/en-us/web/api/window/screenx/index.md</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Validation</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">git diff --check</code>: passed</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45048.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5091109058\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45048\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45048/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45048\">#45048</a></p>",
